Package: bricks
Title: Backend-Agnostic Databricks Data Access
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Alex", "Jakubow", email = "alex.jakubow@dac.nc.gov",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A small, unified interface for reading data from Databricks in R,
    regardless of how you connect. The same handful of verbs work across a
    Databricks SQL warehouse (via 'DBI' and 'odbc'), a native 'sparklyr'
    session inside a Databricks notebook, a remote Databricks Connect session
    (via 'pysparklyr'), and a local CSV extract. Table and SQL handles stay
    lazy so filters, joins, and aggregations push down to Databricks compute,
    and a single collect step pulls a local tibble.
